<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1650" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăhă</span></b> , interj.
		acc. to <i><span class="en">Prisc. 570</span></i> P., primitive of
			the preced., but more rare, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>aha! ah! haha!</i> an exclamation.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of reproof or denial: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aha, tace,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 4, 4, 36</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Rud. 2, 4, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aha, minime,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Bacch. 1, 1, 54</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			laughter, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 4, 7, 11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
